    <string name="more_settings_path_loss">Path-loss exponent (n)</string>
    <string name="more_settings_path_loss_desc">Controls how fast signal fades with distance. Free space is 2.0, a typical home with walls and furniture is 3.0 (the default), and dense walls or many obstructions are 4.0 or more. Higher means signal drops faster over distance.</string>
    <string name="more_settings_path_loss_hint">Lower is more optimistic · Higher is more conservative</string>
    <string name="more_settings_reference_rssi">Reference RSSI at 1 m (A)</string>
    <string name="more_settings_reference_rssi_desc">Signal strength measured 1 metre from your router. Most home routers are −40 to −50 dBm (default −40). Check your router\'s spec sheet, or measure it with the Analyze tab while standing 1 m from the router.</string>
    <string name="more_settings_reference_rssi_hint">Closer to 0 is a stronger router · More negative is weaker</string>
